terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6}÷(2-{3}^{2}) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{6}÷(2-9) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{6}÷(-7) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{(-7)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078453 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "698ccc70-a18b-5b7d-92e2-a87896649ef5" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating Radical Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42836e12-3199-5792-994a-293af74f2ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491581} {:answer/id #uuid "61738bb0-adff-576e-ab79-4270a837a4b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.225" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491628} {:answer/id #uuid "74c48537-34b2-5ccf-ad5e-f4377afc1278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491660} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5aa268-63e4-5c47-9891-92a7d1698d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491673} {:answer/id #uuid "95047847-b017-5a0b-95c7-067528cc8d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95047847-b017-5a0b-95c7-067528cc8d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491711} :answer-field/id #uuid "b57a9137-46c6-56a0-8684-2be92f313fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d8a210d-995e-535a-9fa6-41cb0df374c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-69274" :question/problem "What is the value of $\\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-8+3)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-8+3) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-5) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1+27}+5 & = \\\\ \\sqrt{28}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{28}≈5‭.291\\,503\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{28}+5 & ≈ \\\\ ‭‭‭5.291\\,503+5 & = \\\\ 10.291\\,503 & ≈ \\\\ 10.292\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078453 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "698ccc70-a18b-5b7d-92e2-a87896649ef5" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating Radical Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bed0bff-d019-5504-88a7-69c64217b655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32.398" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491571} {:answer/id #uuid "64b0fd39-89d6-5447-b74f-88923b2bc43c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23.313" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491635} {:answer/id #uuid "acfa8edd-9951-54b8-8c4b-6d2b11e70faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31.231" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491755} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe28402-8834-5efa-8053-bd65c976b296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 